Here are a few notes on the Amiga binaries:

 The unofficial binaries do load in less time (in about 2-4s) than the
 official binaries load the data segment.  The reason is that the
 hunks in the offical binaries are merged (one code hunk, one data, one bss)
 whilst the official ones have circa 200 hunks in them. And the loader
 for the official binaries loads the relocation tables 4 bytes at a time. :)

  If you set the stack you you solve a lot of problems with the crashing.

  I have gotten crashes sometimes at the end of the game (it locks up
  when it asks me to press return after the high score list) when
  running in non-interlace mode.  (I don't know if the screen mode is
  relevent, but I've never had that problem in lace mode).

(I also have problems with getting killed, but thats my fault :) ).

All in all its a great game, although I'd like to see (say in 4.0) an
above ground world (a la Ultima) with multiple dungeons, etc. (Randomly
generated each game, of course.)

